{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791045550,"nonce":"dVshLH68GJRa8KczIWnYPkhqj9U=","title":"Statics and init order: abstract statics, module vars twice, user __init__","message":"- Issue3347: abstracts have no static-variable storage (tast_to_hir.rs `lower_abstract` builds\n  HirAbstractField without static flag or initializer; MIR creates globals only for class statics),\n  so `IntKey.fromList += ..` is computed and discarded. Also an erased `V` passed raw into\n  `Reflect.setField`'s Dynamic slot. (Related: d07fa54.)\n- Issue10845, Issue1810, Issue2614: a packaged entry file that refers to itself compiles twice\n  (`./u/X.hx` and `u/X.hx`); module-level vars get two globals (`lower_global` has no cross-copy\n  dedup) and the second copy loses `@:from` conversions. Related: f0f353a, 91fda9b.\n- Issue9757: a user `static function __init__` is matched as the generated module init by bare name\n  in the codegen startup loops (tiered/llvm/cranelift backends) and runs before the generated init,\n  which then resets every global to its default.","files":null}]}